{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_834fc871f84bd767bfe4df1cc86a58af9e09b4d88a082006f065bcfaef5beb74"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A tracking document reports that `dagger migrate` produced no settings-hint comments in `.dagger/config.toml` on a fresh clone, and that hint introspection failures were logged via slog.Warn without surfacing in default CLI output."}],"claim_ids":["clm_834fc871f84bd767bfe4df1cc86a58af9e09b4d88a082006f065bcfaef5beb74"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T05:10:24Z","created_by_operation":"op_a687a26c5ebc4bedafc943dbe99873d5","id":"pg_85cf625ec48e500b88a768db42eb557b","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/dagger-dagger-migrate-settings-hints-tracking-md-7c35e6274737-68db42eb557b.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_4cadec6be3e559bab441adb74fac51b4"],"title":"dagger/dagger/migrate-settings-hints-tracking.md @ 7c35e6274737","updated_at":"2026-09-14T05:10:24Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a687a26c5ebc4bedafc943dbe99873d5"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_086248ef5f19a63b47e04a84c1bdf7b482a6b01858d7ed067ab46c332d36ab37"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Every operation emits OpenTelemetry spans enriched with logs and metrics; the CLI includes a live TUI and traces can be exported to Jaeger, Honeycomb, or any OTel-compatible backend."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1e6f3b614732ff6c7ae3f62b98bccd4113ba50e3ae08c6b9e851f393fe9a7985"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product ships SDKs in eight languages (Go, Python, TypeScript, PHP, Java, .NET, Elixir, Rust), each generated from the API schema, plus an interactive REPL."},{"claim_ids":["clm_59b369010545209ec952eeffada33e1ff4e0d3e43186baf6c143b19a121b7b97"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Custom object types are content-addressed and can cross SDK and module boundaries without serialization; every operation is keyed by its inputs so only affected operations re-run, with content-addressed caching across local runs and CI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_84814ade7823a272e5849b4b71a5f5426530ab84b13a38cd66b762f21df7fd8a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI can be installed via Homebrew with `brew install dagger/tap/dagger`, and the product runs locally, in CI servers, or in the cloud."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d7651630f5ed41c4ce88358af829f17a99056ade0591290c15a1edbd1c8c5b3f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Dagger is documented as a platform for automating software delivery, providing an execution engine and a system API for orchestrating containers, filesystems, secrets, git repositories, and network tunnels."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e9e4b4e91c4aef35598f73a1b5cd9aa5f8585b9b0c0b9d2e664fefccce4272e7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The only runtime requirement is a Linux container runtime such as Docker; it runs natively on Linux and via Docker Desktop or similar on macOS and Windows, with identical local and CI behavior."}],"claim_ids":["clm_086248ef5f19a63b47e04a84c1bdf7b482a6b01858d7ed067ab46c332d36ab37","clm_1e6f3b614732ff6c7ae3f62